WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.080
- Well, we've talked about this before,

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.390
but you started acting when
you were pretty young, right?

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:04.223
- Yeah.

00:00:04.223 --> 00:00:05.970
- I kind of heard crazy stories of like

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.630
how you used to be like young
and like travel to New York,

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.060
like without parents.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.490
- Yeah, so I grew up in Maine

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.970
and I started auditioning for
like Broadway shows and stuff,

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.530
when I was like 10 and around,

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.760
and basically that would mean my parents

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.950
would have to drive me
like five hours to New York

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.720
for like one audition and then come home,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.080
which was just not sustainable.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.870
You know, they both worked full time.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.043
And so eventually like around 12,

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.780
my brother was like 14 and they were like,

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.110
you guys can get on a Greyhound
bus and go to New York city

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.100
and come back and you'll be fine.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.620
- Not a Dateline special
in the waiting at all.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.030
Yeah, no.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:41.010
- But yeah. So when I went and
auditioned for high society,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.410
which was the show that I
eventually did, they, you know,

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.820
get on a Greyhound bus with my brother,

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.790
I auditioned and they're like, okay.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.690
So we want to call you back
for tomorrow. Very exciting.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.010
And they were like, so we'll,
we'll see you tomorrow.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:54.990
And I was like, yes, you will.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.240
Because I live here. Totally.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.350
Absolutely.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:01.340
I'm not a homeless street
rat running around the

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.620
streets of New York.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:06.560
So my parents like faxed a credit card,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.450
a copy of the credit card to a hotel.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.600
And they were like, our
children will be checking in

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.820
and then we'll be along shortly

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.380
because obviously we're
not terrible parents

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.920
who've let them go to New York.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:15.753
- Oh my gosh, I love your parents.

00:01:15.753 --> 00:01:16.830
- And so we were like, you know, walk in.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.180
And we're like, yes, our
parents will be along shortly.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.440
And like, we're like,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.080
wash our socks and underwear in the sink.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.060
And then like, just go
back in the next day.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.630
And like just all the
while pretending like, yes,

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:30.500
I am a totally normal person
who lives here and I'm not.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.380
- I just came from my home.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.213
- Yeah.

00:01:32.213 --> 00:01:34.090
- Your brother's awesome, to
take you to the, it's so cool.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:34.923
- It's so cool.

00:01:34.923 --> 00:01:37.330
We're not gonna applause for my brother.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.850
- And I mean, that's just so funny,

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:39.840
cause like when you have kids,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.530
I'm going to ask you if
you would allow your kid.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.240
Cause I would never allow
my kids to do what I did

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.506
when I was young.

00:01:44.506 --> 00:01:46.900
- I wouldn't even allow
my kids to be sick on me

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.030
the way that you were.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:49.743
- I know, you would.

00:01:49.743 --> 00:01:51.500
- So, maybe I'd be the kind
of person who would be like

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.100
have fun, sweetie, bye.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:55.023
Good luck.

